|name2 = King of Extinction Phono
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''King of Extinction Phono''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Unlike [[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]], King of Extinction Phono is more of a supportive unit, lacking any damage-boosting abilities but packing a 2-second Slow.

Notably, the slow provides just under 28% uptime and should be considered complementary crowd-controlling. Multiple hits from the multi-hit or Mini-Surge land on a given enemy will still not perma-Slow. However, this extra utility still works on many mixed stages since this effect applies to all enemies. Additionally, Dark Phono's massive LD coverage allows him to Slow a huge portion of the field. Dark Phono's immunity to curse means that they work even against [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]] and the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]], and immunity to waves and surges are great to have in endgame.

Additionally, this unit still features impressive stats for a high-range sniper, though the multi-hit and separate LD ranges make these stats difficult, although easier than normal Phonoa's, to utilize since they only overlap in 490-550 (60 width). However, if a target gets damage KB from on the 1st or 2nd hit could make the 3rd miss due to hitboxes disappearing during a damage KB. The Mini-Surges can add some extra damage and apply slow procs to any enemies hit by it though a bit inconsistent due to Surge spawn points, so it should be considered a small bonus.

Finally, this unit has higher HP and base attack than Phonoa in exchange for 100 range. However, 500 standing range reaching up to 900 is still impressive and allows this unit to outrange and snipe many enemies nonetheless. Not even waves and surges can go past this range advantage. The minimum that enemies are guaranteed to take is 17k damage and 2.4k DPS with the potential to triple that amount if the enemy is exactly at 490-550 range. Dark Phono's standing range, decent DPS, immunities, and slow procs on enemies makes him a great flexible pull for most content with no hard counter.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Sniper}}

